    "historicalInfo": "Gaddi's opened in 1953 at The Peninsula Hong Kong, one of Asia's grandest colonial-era hotels (opened 1928). Named for founding restaurant director Leo Gaddi, it has been a pillar of Hong Kong's fine dining scene for over 70 years, hosting royalty, heads of state, and celebrities.",
