        "narration": "Welcome to Gaddi's, Hong Kong's most storied fine dining institution! Opened in 1953 within The Peninsula—Asia's most celebrated colonial-era hotel—Gaddi's has hosted royalty, heads of state, and decades of Hong Kong's most important occasions. Beneath glittering chandeliers and amid impeccably set linen-draped tables, classically trained chefs craft contemporary French cuisine with subtle Asian nuances, paired with an extraordinary cellar. Whether for a special dinner or the legendary Peninsula Lobby High Tea, this is Hong Kong at its most magnificently refined.",
