    "historicalInfo": "According to Greek mythology, Delos was the birthplace of twin gods Apollo and Artemis. From the 9th century BCE it grew into the Aegean's foremost religious and commercial hub. At its height in the 2nd century BCE, over 30,000 people lived on the tiny island. It was declared a UNESCO World Heritage Site in 1990.",
