    "historicalInfo": "Built between 1898 and 1900 during the Klondike Gold Rush, the White Pass & Yukon Route Railway was designated an American Society of Civil Engineers Historic Civil Engineering Landmark in 1994. It transported over 100,000 gold-rush stampeding prospectors over the White Pass.",
