    "historicalInfo": "The Bonanza Bar & Grill occupies a historic Gold Rush-era building on Skagway's Broadway Street. The name 'Bonanza' references the famous Bonanza Creek where gold was first discovered in the Klondike in 1896, triggering the stampede that gave birth to Skagway.",
    "yearBuilt": null,
