    "narration": "Stroll through Europe's largest outdoor market, stretching 260 metres through De Pijp neighbourhood. Fresh stroopwafels, herring, flowers, cheese, and street food line the stalls — the true taste of Amsterdam daily life.",
    "description": "Europe's largest outdoor street market — 260m of Dutch street food and goods",
    "category": "Market",
    "detailedDescription": "Open since 1905, Albert Cuyp Market runs Monday to Saturday from 9am to 5pm with around 260 stalls. Try fresh raw herring (haring) with onions, warm stroopwafels straight off the iron, Dutch cheese, and Indonesian street food reflecting Amsterdam's multicultural heritage. The surrounding De Pijp district has Amsterdam's best neighbourhood restaurants and coffee bars.",
