    "narration": "Gamla Stan is Stockholm's medieval old town, founded in the 13th century on a small island. Its narrow cobblestone streets, ochre and terracotta facades, and the Stortorget square — scene of the Stockholm Bloodbath of 1520 — make it Scandinavia's best-preserved medieval city centre.",
    "description": "Stockholm's medieval island old town — 13th-century streets, royal palace, Nobel Museum",
    "category": "Historic District",
    "detailedDescription": "Gamla Stan sits on Stadsholmen island where Stockholm was founded in 1252. The Stortorget square, the city's oldest, was where King Christian II of Denmark executed 90 Swedish nobles in 1520 in the Stockholm Bloodbath — a pivotal moment leading to Swedish independence. The Royal Palace dominates the northern end with 1,430 rooms, the largest royal palace in the world still used as an official residence. The Nobel Prize Museum on Stortorget presents every laureate. Wander down Mårten Trotzigs Gränd, the narrowest alley (90cm wide), for an atmospheric experience.",
