    "narration": "Strøget is one of Europe's longest pedestrian shopping streets, stretching 1.1 kilometres from City Hall Square to Kongens Nytorv. Opened to pedestrians in 1962, it now hosts everything from H&M to Royal Copenhagen porcelain.",
    "description": "Europe's longest pedestrian shopping street — 1.1 km of shops, cafés, and street life",
    "category": "Shopping",
    "detailedDescription": "Strøget ('the stroll') was closed to traffic in August 1962 over shopkeepers' fierce objections — they feared losing business. Within a year, sales rose 40%. Today it connects five squares: Rådhuspladsen, Gammel Torv, Nytorv, Amagertorv, and Kongens Nytorv. Look for the Stork Fountain at Amagertorv, a Copenhagen meeting point since 1894. Royal Copenhagen's flagship store on Amagertorv sells hand-painted porcelain using techniques unchanged since 1775.",
