    "id": "amsterdam_bike_rental_tour",
    "cityId": "amsterdam",
    "name": "Amsterdam Bike Tour",
    "lat": 52.3791,
    "lng": 4.898,
    "radius": 200,
    "narration": "See Amsterdam like a local — by bicycle. Guided bike tours take you through the historic centre, past windmills, through the Jordaan, and along peaceful canal paths that cars can't reach. Amsterdam is the world's most bike-friendly city.",
    "description": "Guided cycling tour through Amsterdam's historic canals and neighbourhoods",
    "category": "Activity",
    "detailedDescription": "With 881,000 bicycles and more bikes than people, Amsterdam is the world capital of cycling. Guided bike tours typically cover 15–20 km over 3 hours, visiting the medieval centre, Jewish Quarter, Plantage neighbourhood, and scenic canal belts. Operators also offer self-guided rentals with GPS audio guides perfect for cruise visitors. Most shops are near Centraal Station.",
