    "id": "bangkok_chatuchak_market",
    "cityId": "bangkok",
    "name": "Chatuchak Weekend Market",
    "lat": 13.7999,
    "lng": 100.5506,
    "radius": 300,
    "narration": "Chatuchak Market is the world's largest weekend market, with 15,000 stalls spread over 35 acres. Every weekend 200,000 visitors browse antiques, vintage clothing, street food, ceramics, and live animals across 27 themed sections.",
    "description": "World's largest weekend market — 15,000 stalls, 200,000 visitors, antiques to street food",
    "category": "Market",
    "detailedDescription": "Established in 1942, Chatuchak (JJ Market) operates every Saturday and Sunday 09:00-18:00. The market is divided into 27 sections with coloured-coded maps available at the entrances. Section 2-4 specialises in antiques and art; Section 8-11 in clothing and accessories; Section 22-26 in plants and ceramics. The food section in the centre serves some of Bangkok's best value street food — grilled pork skewers, mango salad, pad see ew, and refreshing young coconut water. Live animals including exotic birds and reptiles are sold (controversially) in a dedicated section. The market connects to the BTS Skytrain and MRT Chatuchak Park stations.",
