    "narration": "Relax in Amsterdam's beloved Vondelpark, a 47-hectare green oasis in the heart of the city. Locals cycle, picnic, and enjoy open-air concerts here, especially on sunny days when the park buzzes with life.",
    "description": "Amsterdam's most beloved 47-hectare urban park with open-air theatre",
    "category": "Park",
    "detailedDescription": "Vondelpark is Amsterdam's answer to Central Park — a beloved green space where Amsterdammers come to cycle, sunbathe, and socialise. The park features rose gardens, ponds, playgrounds, and the Open Air Theatre hosting free performances in summer. It borders the Museum Quarter, making it an ideal place to rest between Rijksmuseum and Van Gogh Museum visits. The park sees 10 million visitors annually.",
