    "narration": "Visit Keukenhof, the world's largest flower garden and the crown jewel of Dutch spring. Over 7 million tulips, daffodils, and hyacinths bloom across 32 hectares from mid-March through May — a once-in-a-lifetime spectacle.",
    "description": "World's largest flower garden — 7 million spring bulbs across 32 hectares (Mar–May)",
    "category": "Park",
    "detailedDescription": "Open only 8 weeks a year, Keukenhof showcases over 800 tulip varieties along with daffodils, hyacinths, and orchids. The gardens include 15 pavilions with elaborate floral displays, a windmill, and a boat tour through the surrounding bulb fields. From Amsterdam, direct bus connections run from Schiphol Airport (30 min). Evening Glow events in April offer illuminated night garden experiences.",
