    "narration": "The Van Gogh Museum holds the world's largest collection of Vincent van Gogh's works, including Sunflowers and The Bedroom. Walk through the passionate and turbulent life of one of history's most beloved painters.",
    "description": "World's largest Van Gogh collection — 200 paintings, 500 drawings",
    "category": "Museum",
    "detailedDescription": "With over 200 paintings, 500 drawings and 750 letters by Vincent van Gogh, this museum offers the most complete view of the artist's life and work. The chronological layout traces Van Gogh's evolution from dark Dutch landscapes to the brilliant colors of his Arles period. The Bedroom, Wheatfield with Crows, and multiple Sunflowers versions are here. Book tickets well in advance — queues can be hours long.",
