    "detailedDescription": "The Anne Frank House preserves the secret annex (Achterhuis) at Prinsengracht 263, where Anne Frank, her family, and four others hid from July 1942 to August 1944. Anne's original diary is displayed alongside photographs and documents. The museum opened in 1960 at Otto Frank's request. Timed-entry tickets must be booked online weeks in advance — walk-up entry is rarely possible.",
