    "narration": "Sentosa Island — once a British military fortress — is Singapore's entertainment island, home to Universal Studios Singapore, Adventure Cove Waterpark, S.E.A. Aquarium, three beaches, and the Resorts World casino. A cable car and boardwalk connect it to the mainland.",
    "description": "Singapore's entertainment island — Universal Studios, beaches, cable car from HarbourFront",
    "category": "Theme Park",
    "detailedDescription": "Sentosa (from Malay 'peace and tranquillity') was renamed ironically after its wartime role — it was previously Pulau Belakang Mati (Island of Death Behind) for piracy-related deaths. Fort Siloso, the preserved WWII coastal battery that faced the wrong direction when Japan invaded by land in 1942, is a sobering museum. Universal Studios Singapore, the only one in Southeast Asia, has rides based on Transformers, Jurassic Park, and Hollywood films. Palawan Beach extends to a tiny peninsula that is the southernmost point of continental Asia. The Skyline Luge and Mega Adventure zipline cross the island's forested hillside.",
