    "radius": 100,
    "narration": "Charles Bridge is Prague's most iconic landmark, a 516-metre Gothic bridge across the Vltava River lined with 30 Baroque statues of saints. Construction began in 1357 at exactly 5:31 AM on July 9th — the Emperor chose this moment for its numerological significance: 135797531.",
    "description": "Prague's 1357 Gothic bridge with 30 Baroque saint statues — sunrise walk is magical",
    "category": "Landmark",
    "detailedDescription": "Emperor Charles IV laid the foundation stone in 1357 at a numerologically auspicious moment — the sequence 1-3-5-7-9-7-5-3-1 is a palindrome that was believed to strengthen the bridge. For 400 years it was Prague's only river crossing. The 30 Baroque statues (added 1683–1714) include a gilded Latin cross inscription, Saint John of Nepomuk (whose touching brings luck), and groups of remarkable artistic quality. At dawn, before tourists arrive, the bridge and its tower reflections in the still river create an unforgettable scene. Street musicians often play on the bridge throughout the day.",
