    "detailedDescription": "Christian IV, Denmark's most prolific builder-king, used Rosenborg as his summer palace. The castle's three towers and copper spires create a fairy-tale silhouette in the King's Garden. The basement treasury holds the crown jewels — King Christian V's crown of 1670 set with 2,000 diamonds, rubies, and sapphires is the centrepiece. The throne room features three life-sized silver lions. The castle has never been conquered and its collections have remained largely intact for 400 years.",
