    "narration": "Holmenkollen ski jump towers 417 metres above sea level on Oslo's forested hillside, offering the most dramatic view of the Norwegian capital and its fjord. The world's oldest ski museum beneath tells 4,000 years of skiing history.",
    "description": "Oslo's iconic ski jump with world's oldest ski museum and panoramic fjord views",
    "category": "Landmark",
    "detailedDescription": "Holmenkollen hosted its first ski jump competition in 1892 and has been rebuilt 19 times since. The current structure, designed for the 2011 World Championships, is an architectural icon. The jump tower's observation deck gives a 360° view from Oslo city to the Oslofjord islands. The ski museum underground documents skiing from Stone Age petroglyphs showing prehistoric skiers, through Polar explorer Fridtjof Nansen's 1888 Greenland crossing on skis, to modern Olympic champions. A zip-line from the top of the jump tower to the stadium below is Oslo's most thrilling experience.",
