    "narration": "Skansen is the world's oldest open-air museum, founded in 1891 to preserve Sweden's rural past. Across 75 hectares, 150 historical buildings from every Swedish region were relocated here, complete with costumed craftspeople and Scandinavian wildlife.",
    "description": "World's oldest open-air museum (1891) — 150 historical buildings and Scandinavian zoo",
    "category": "Museum",
    "detailedDescription": "Arthur Hazelius founded Skansen in 1891 after noticing traditional Swedish life disappearing with industrialisation. Farm homesteads, windmills, a glassblower, a druggist, and craftspeople in period costume populate the hillside. The Skansen Aquarium houses monkeys and alligators. The Nordic Zoo displays lynx, wolverines, moose, reindeer, wolves, and brown bears in naturalistic enclosures. The Sami camp represents Sweden's indigenous Sámi people with their reindeer. Skansen hosts Sweden's biggest Midsummer and Walpurgis Night celebrations.",
