    "lng": 18.0914,
    "radius": 80,
    "narration": "The Vasa Museum houses a 64-gun warship that sank on its maiden voyage in 1628 and was salvaged intact in 1961. It is the world's best-preserved 17th-century ship and the most visited museum in Scandinavia with 1.5 million visitors a year.",
    "description": "World's only preserved 17th-century warship — sank 1628, salvaged 1961",
    "category": "Museum",
    "detailedDescription": "The warship Vasa was the most powerful vessel of its time — 69 metres long, 52.5 metres tall, decorated with 700 sculptures. It capsized after sailing just 1,300 metres, killing 30 people, because it was too narrow for its height and carried too many cannon. The cold, brackish Baltic water preserved the oak hull remarkably. The salvage in 1961 was one of history's great maritime engineering feats. 98% of the ship is original. Scientists found the remains of at least 15 crew members and personal effects including backgammon sets and a sailor's chest containing his best Sunday clothes.",
