    "narration": "ABBA The Museum on Djurgården island is the world's only official ABBA museum, celebrating the Swedish pop group that has sold over 400 million records. Step into the studio where Waterloo and Dancing Queen were recorded, and sing on a virtual stage with all four members.",
    "description": "World's only official ABBA museum — interactive exhibits and virtual concerts",
    "category": "Museum",
    "detailedDescription": "The interactive museum contains original costumes, instruments, gold records, and stage set-ups from ABBA's peak years 1972–1982. A private phone booth in the museum connects directly to Benny Andersson who designed the experience — he calls at random moments. Visitors receive an interactive wristband keyed to their personal profile, and can step onstage to sing and dance with holograms of Agnetha, Björn, Benny, and Anni-Frid. The museum sits inside the Swedish Music Hall of Fame on Djurgården, easily reached by ferry from the cruise terminal.",
