    "narration": "The new Munch Museum opened in 2021 in a dramatic 13-storey tilting tower at the Oslofjord. It holds the largest collection of Edvard Munch's works — 26,000 objects donated by the artist himself to the City of Oslo upon his death in 1944.",
    "description": "World's largest Munch collection — 26,000 works in a dramatic fjord-side tower",
    "category": "Museum",
    "detailedDescription": "Edvard Munch gave everything to Oslo when he died — 1,788 paintings, 4,443 drawings, 15,391 prints, 13,000 photographs, and his library. The new Lambda building by Spanish architects Estudio Herreros rises at an angle over the harbour, its perforated aluminium facade referencing traditional Norwegian curtains and the play of Nordic light. The permanent collection spans Munch's full career from early realism to his late expressionist 'mountain man' period after his 1908 breakdown. Multiple versions of The Scream, Vampire, Madonna, and The Kiss are on display. The 13th floor restaurant has unmatched fjord views.",
