    "historicalInfo": "Established in 1910, Sitka National Historical Park is one of Alaska's oldest federal parks. It commemorates the 1804 Battle of Sitka, where Russian forces defeated Tlingit warriors who had previously destroyed a Russian fort in 1802. The park contains 18 totem poles and a visitor center with Indigenous art demonstrations.",
