    "radius": 80,
    "narration": "The Royal Museums of Fine Arts in Brussels hold one of the world's great collections of Flemish masters, including the world's largest collection of works by Pieter Bruegel the Elder and masterpieces by Rubens, Van Dyck, and Memling. The Magritte Museum inside holds 200 works by Belgium's surrealist icon.",
    "description": "World's largest Bruegel collection + Magritte Museum — Flemish masters in royal palaces",
    "category": "Museum",
    "detailedDescription": "The complex encompasses six museums: Ancient Art (15th-18th centuries), Modern Art, Magritte Museum, Fin-de-Siècle Museum, Meunier Museum, and Wiertz Museum. The Bruegel collection includes The Census at Bethlehem, The Fall of the Rebel Angels, and The Adoration of the Magi. The Magritte Museum, housed in the Hotel Altenloh, displays 200 works chronologically — including the famous Man in Bowler Hat and Empire of Light. The underground passages connecting the neoclassical buildings form a labyrinthine museum city. The Coudenberg archaeological site beneath reveals the ruins of the Habsburg palace where Charles V abdicated in 1555.",
