    "historicalInfo": "Dog sledding has been central to Alaska Native cultures for over 2,000 years as a means of transportation, hunting, and trade. Today, glacier dog sledding near Skagway combines Alaska's ancient mushing tradition with modern helicopter access to remote glacial terrain.",
