    "narration": "Brussels hosts the headquarters of the European Union — the European Parliament, the European Commission in the Berlaymont building, and the Council of the EU. Together with NATO HQ also in Brussels, this makes the city the de facto capital of Europe.",
    "description": "EU capital of Europe — Parliament, Commission (Berlaymont), Council, and NATO HQ",
    "category": "District",
    "detailedDescription": "The Berlaymont building — distinctive X-shaped and clad in glass — has been the European Commission headquarters since 1967. The European Parliament, with its 705 MEPs, meets in a crescent-shaped building nicknamed 'les capotes' (the condoms) by irreverent Belgians. The Parlamentarium visitor centre offers free interactive tours of how the EU works. Museum Espace Léopold, the free visitor gallery inside the Parliament, gives direct views of the hemicycle. The Parc du Cinquantenaire nearby has the monumental arch built for Belgium's 50th independence anniversary and houses three fine museums.",
