        "name": "Mendenhall Glacier",
        "narration": "Stand before the awe-inspiring Mendenhall Glacier and feel the raw power of Alaska's wilderness. This massive river of ice stretches 13 miles, its blue-green walls glowing in the sunlight. The roar of calving ice and the rush of glacial meltwater into Mendenhall Lake creates an unforgettable sensory experience. Black bears and bald eagles make their home along these shores, and salmon battle upstream in the clear glacial streams.",
        "description": "A 13-mile glacier near Juneau within Tongass National Forest, one of Alaska's most visited natural wonders."
