    "historicalInfo": "Akrotiri was a flourishing Minoan port city destroyed by the Theran eruption around 1627 BCE. Unlike Pompeii, no human remains were found, suggesting residents evacuated before the catastrophe. Excavations began in 1967 under Prof. Spyridon Marinatos.",
